msgid ""
"We can now retrieve and analyze the results from the Sampler job. We start "
"by plotting results from the noiseless simulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na nating kunin at suriin ang mga resulta mula sa Sampler job. "
"Magsisimula tayo sa pag-plot ng mga resulta mula sa noiseless na "
"simulation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/error-"
"detection/extracted-outputs/4741910b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/error-"
"detection/extracted-outputs/4741910b-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As expected, the check qubit doesn't detect any errors. Next, we plot "
"results from the noisy simulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng inaasahan, hindi nakakakita ng anumang error ang check qubit. "
"Susunod, i-plot natin ang mga resulta mula sa noisy na simulation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/error-"
"detection/extracted-outputs/51a8f3d9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/error-"
"detection/extracted-outputs/51a8f3d9-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we can see, some measurements captured the error by flagging the check qubit as \"1\", which are visible in the last four columns. These shots are discarded.\n"
"Note: The ancilla qubit can also introduce new errors to the circuit. To reduce the effect of this, we can insert nested checks with additional ancilla qubits to the quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng makikita natin, ilang mga sukat ang nakuha ang error sa pamamagitan ng pagmamarka ng check qubit bilang \"1\", na makikita sa huling apat na hanay. Ang mga shot na ito ay itatapon.\n"
"Paalala: Ang ancilla qubit ay maaari ring magdulot ng mga bagong error sa circuit. Upang mabawasan ang epekto nito, maaari tayong maglagay ng mga nested check na may karagdagang ancilla qubits sa quantum circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa malalaking hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem-1}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we demonstrate a significant task for quantum computing algorithms, "
"which is preparing a GHZ state. We will demonstrate how to do this on a real"
" backend using error detection.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinakita na namin ngayon ang isang mahalagang gawain para sa mga quantum "
"computing algorithm, at ito ay ang paghahanda ng GHZ state. Ipapakita namin "
"kung paano gawin ito sa isang tunay na backend gamit ang pagdetekta ng "
"error.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The error detection algorithm for GHZ state preparation respects the "
"hardware topology. We begin by selecting the desired hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang error detection algorithm para sa paghahanda ng GHZ state ay iginagalang"
" ang hardware topology. Nagsisimula tayo sa pagpili ng nais na hardware.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A GHZ state on $n$ qubits is defined as\n"
"$$\\lvert \\mathrm{GHZ}_n\\rangle \\;=\\; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(\\lvert 0\\rangle^{\\otimes n} \\,+\\, \\lvert 1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\\Big).$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang GHZ state sa $n$ qubits ay tinukoy bilang\n"
"$$\\lvert \\mathrm{GHZ}_n\\rangle \\;=\\; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(\\lvert 0\\rangle^{\\otimes n} \\,+\\, \\lvert 1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\\Big).$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A very naive approach to prepare the GHZ state would be to choose a root "
"qubit with an initial Hadamard gate, which puts the qubit to an equal "
"superposition state, and then to entangle this qubit with every other qubit."
" This is not a good approach, since it requires long-range and deep CNOT "
"interactions. In this tutorial, we will use multiple techniques alongside "
"error detection to reliably prepare the GHZ state on real hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang napaka-simpleng paraan upang ihanda ang GHZ state ay ang pumili ng"
" isang root qubit na may paunang Hadamard gate, na naglalagay ng qubit sa "
"isang pantay na superposition state, at pagkatapos ay i-entangle ang qubit "
"na ito sa bawat isa pang qubit. Hindi ito isang magandang pamamaraan, dahil "
"nangangailangan ito ng mahabang-distansya at malalim na CNOT na interaksyon."
" Sa tutorial na ito, gagamitin namin ang maraming teknik kasabay ng "
"pagdetekta ng error upang mapagkakatiwalaang ihanda ang GHZ state sa tunay "
"na hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution-1}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Map the GHZ state to hardware {#map-the-ghz-state-to-hardware}"
msgstr "I-map ang GHZ state sa hardware {#map-the-ghz-state-to-hardware}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we search for a root to map the GHZ circuit on hardware. We remove "
"edges/nodes whose CZ errors, measurement errors, and $T_2$ values are worse "
"than the thresholds below. These will not be included in the GHZ circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, naghahanap tayo ng isang root para i-map ang GHZ circuit sa hardware. "
"Tinatanggal natin ang mga edge/node na ang kanilang mga CZ error, "
"measurement error, at $T_2$ na halaga ay mas malala kaysa sa mga threshold "
"sa ibaba. Hindi sila isasama sa GHZ circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the function below, we construct the GHZ circuit on the chosen "
"hardware starting from the root and using breadth-first search (BFS).\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang function sa ibaba, binubuo natin ang GHZ circuit sa piniling "
"hardware simula sa root at gumagamit ng breadth-first search (BFS).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now repeatedly search for the best root, where the GHZ circuit will "
"originate from.\n"
msgstr ""
"Paulit-ulit na naghahanap tayo ng pinakamahusay na root, kung saan "
"magsisimula ang GHZ circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now construct the GHZ circuit starting from a specific node - as in, the "
"best root - searching for the shortest depth using breadth-first search.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binubuo na natin ngayon ang GHZ circuit simula sa isang tiyak na node — ang "
"pinakamahusay na root — naghahanap ng pinakamaikling depth gamit ang "
"breadth-first search.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We need one final consideration before inserting valid checks. This is "
"related to the concept of \"coverage\", which is a measure of how many of "
"the wires in a quantum circuit a check can cover. With a higher coverage, we"
" can detect errors on a wider part of the circuit. With this measure, we can"
" select among the valid checks with the highest circuit coverage. In other "
"words, we will be using the `weighted_coverage` function to score different "
"checks for the GHZ circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kailangan pa nating isaalang-alang ang isang huling bagay bago maglagay ng "
"mga wastong check. Ito ay may kaugnayan sa konsepto ng \"coverage\", na "
"isang sukatan ng kung gaano karaming wire sa isang quantum circuit ang "
"maaaring saklawin ng isang check. Sa mas mataas na coverage, mas malawak na "
"bahagi ng circuit ang ating matutukoy na may error. Sa pamamagitan ng "
"sukatan na ito, maaari tayong pumili sa mga wastong check na may "
"pinakamataas na circuit coverage. Sa ibang salita, gagamitin natin ang "
"`weighted_coverage` na function para i-score ang iba't ibang check para sa "
"GHZ circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now insert checks to the GHZ circuit. Finding valid checks is very "
"convenient for the GHZ state, since any two-qubit Pauli $Z$ operator $Z_i "
"Z_j$ acting on any two qubits $i,j$ of the GHZ circuit is a support and "
"therefore a valid check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na nating ipasok ang mga check sa GHZ circuit. Ang paghahanap ng mga "
"wastong check ay napaka-maginhawa para sa GHZ state, dahil ang anumang two-"
"qubit Pauli $Z$ operator na $Z_i Z_j$ na kumikilos sa anumang dalawang qubit"
" na $i,j$ ng GHZ circuit ay isang suporta at samakatuwid ay isang wastong "
"check.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Also note that the checks in this case are controlled-$Z$ operators "
"neighboring Hadamard gates from the left and right on the ancilla qubit. "
"This is equivalent to a CNOT gate applied to the ancilla qubit. The code "
"below inserts the checks into the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin din na ang mga check sa kasong ito ay controlled-$Z$ operators na "
"kalapit ng mga Hadamard gates mula sa kaliwa at kanan ng ancilla qubit. Ito "
"ay katumbas ng isang CNOT gate na inilapat sa ancilla qubit. Ang code sa "
"ibaba ay nagpapasok ng mga check sa circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now print out the qubits used in the GHZ circuit and the check "
"qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na nating i-print ang mga qubit na ginagamit sa GHZ circuit at ang "
"mga check qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can also print out some error statistics.\n"
msgstr "Maaari din nating i-print ang ilang mga istatistika ng error.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As previously, we can simulate the circuit first in the absence of noise to "
"ensure correctness of the GHZ state preparation circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng dati, maaari nating i-simulate ang circuit nang una sa kawalan ng "
"ingay upang matiyak ang kawastuhan ng GHZ state preparation circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/error-"
"detection/extracted-outputs/b905e875-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/error-"
"detection/extracted-outputs/b905e875-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As expected, the check qubits are measured as all zeros, and we successfully"
" prepared the GHZ state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng inaasahan, ang mga check qubit ay nasusukat bilang lahat ng sero, "
"at matagumpay nating nahanda ang GHZ state.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives-1}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we are ready to run the circuit on real hardware and demonstrate how the"
" error detection protocol can capture errors in GHZ state preparation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Handa na tayo ngayon na patakbuhin ang circuit sa tunay na hardware at "
"ipakita kung paano nakakakuha ng mga error ang error detection protocol sa "
"paghahanda ng GHZ state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We define a helper function to add measurements to the GHZ circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
